  "body": "https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#mutation-observer-compound-microtask-queued-flag\nMissing initial state for this flag, just add \"(initially unset)\", whe have this for other flags (in this spec and in other spec):\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#stop-propagation-flag\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-listener\nhttps://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#textdecoder\nhttps://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#gbk-flag\nhttps://url.spec.whatwg.org/#non-relative-flag\n\n---\n\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#registered-observer\nWhy we don't have definition for \"observer\", \"options\" and \"source\" with some id? Instead using `<b>` in other place for this terms it would be more convenient to use references. \n\n---\n\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-mutationrecord\n`readonly attribute Node target;` << this IDL should not be mark by `[SameObject]`? It's not change, similarly what we have for root in NodeIterator/TreeWalker (https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-nodeiterator, https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-treewalker)\n",
